{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JsBksXyeXaMb9DSKrF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. Before I draft, I have a few questions. Your answers would change what the summary says, and I'd rather not guess:\n\n1. **Where will the other $33,000 a year come from?** The attorney costs $78,000 a year and the foundation caps awards at $45,000. Reviewers will spot that gap right away. Is part of the county's $60,000 going to cover it, or another funder, or reserves? And is that money committed or still pending?\n\n2. **Has the county contract been renewed?** If the October you mentioned was last month, what happened? If it's October 2027, how confident are you that it will be renewed? That tells me whether to present county funding as stable or leave it out of the match.\n\n3. **When the attorney leaves in June, will you rehire for that spot from other funds?** If not, this grant would really keep you at two attorneys, not take you to three. That's a different case to make, and the foundation will want it stated honestly. Which is it?\n\n4. **How many cases does one attorney close in a year?** \"About 80 open at a time\" doesn't tell me that. With a yearly figure I can say how many more tenants a third attorney would serve, for example \"roughly X of the 300 we now turn away.\" If you don't have it, I'll leave the projection out instead of estimating.\n\n5. **Does the foundation give guidelines for the summary?** For example, required sections or scoring criteria. And what are the clinic's name and county?\n\nIf you don't know some of these, say so and I'll write around them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":248,"cache_read_input_tokens":9566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":248},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed